# The root .gitignore has a bare `model/` rule for the top-level dev directory.
# A bare rule matches at every depth, so it also swallowed `go/pkg/model/` — the
# package holding the download/cache manager was never committed, and a fresh
# clone could not build the Go SDK at all. Re-include it here.
!pkg/model/
!pkg/model/**

# Build output; the runtime is not vendored. See the ONNX Runtime section of
# README.md for how the shared library is located.
lib/
*.so
*.dylib

# `go build ./cmd/monocr` run from go/ writes this binary; a stale 9.7 MB
# linux/amd64 build of it was committed in 37ded04. Anchored, because a bare
# `monocr` would also ignore cmd/monocr/.
/monocr
